# 4. LIVE LOCATION AND GEOSPATIAL ENGINE

This is one of the most important parts of the application.

Implement a proper browser Geolocation API integration.

Requirements:

1. Request location permission when the user activates a location-dependent feature.
2. Detect the actual current latitude and longitude.
3. Retrieve accurate location coordinates from the browser.
4. Display location acquisition status.
5. Display the detected coordinates and resolved address.
6. Reverse-geocode coordinates into a readable address.
7. Show the user's location on an interactive map.
8. Allow users to manually adjust their pin.
9. Provide a location search box.
10. Allow custom radius selection: 500 m, 1 km, 2 km, 5 km and 10 km.
11. Update nearby results when the location or radius changes.
12. Calculate distances using geographic coordinates.
13. Filter nearby results using actual distance.
14. Provide map markers for nearby issues, vehicles, garbage bins and transport stops.
15. Implement location refresh.
16. Handle permission denial, timeout and unavailable location.
17. Provide manual address and map-pin fallback.
18. Prevent invalid coordinates and inaccurate location claims.
19. Store coordinates with appropriate timestamps and accuracy metadata.
20. Use geospatial database queries where supported.

The system must never substitute a random city location when GPS fails.

Use location data only with appropriate user permission.

Important: Do not claim background location tracking when the browser cannot support it. Implement foreground location updates and explicitly explain tracking limitations.

Map requirements:

- Interactive map.
- Zoom and pan.
- Current location marker.
- Nearby places.
- Custom radius.
- Category filters.
- Marker clustering.
- Map/list view switching.
- Directions through supported map services.
- Loading and error states.

Use a properly configured mapping provider such as Google Maps, Mapbox or OpenStreetMap with an appropriate routing/geocoding provider.

Do not hardcode a map image as a substitute for an interactive map.

